vice": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018CgvrjWxXnDiDkCZSD3Apd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012A5GWBKMbYfmuagAFYXyaC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging and was not considered as a rollback target. Next steps: confirm error rate recovery, investigate the v2.3.1 failure, and decide when it is safe to redeploy a fixed build.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was only deployed to staging, so I did not use it.\n- **Approval:** No change-manager approval was needed, since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened a SEV2 incident titled \"checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0\". Its summary describes the failure, the rollback, and the next steps: confirm recovery, investigate v2.3.1, and decide when a fixed build is safe to redeploy. The incident tool reported it as executed.\n\nThe incident is open and will page the on-call engineer. The v2.3.1 failure still needs investigation before anything is redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}